<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">14 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 14 September, from 775 to 1982.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">775 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,251 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Leo IV the Khazar becomes Byzantine emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leo-iv-the-khazar">Leo IV the Khazar</a>, co-emperor since 751, became senior emperor after his father Constantine V died while campaigning against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgars">Bulgars</a>. Leo, whose byname came from his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazar</a> mother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tzitzak">Tzitzak</a>, reigned until his death in 780.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leo-iv-the-khazar">Leo IV the Khazar</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">786 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,240 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Harun al-Rashid becomes Abbasid caliph</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the night his brother al-Hadi died, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harun-al-rashid">Harun al-Rashid</a> became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>. His reign, remembered through the Thousand and One Nights, marked a high point of Abbasid power and culture.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harun-al-rashid">Harun al-Rashid</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/919">919 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,107 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Vikings of Dublin defeat Niall Glúndub at Islandbridge</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A coalition of native Irish led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niall-glundub">Niall Glúndub</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/high-king-of-ireland">High King of Ireland</a>, tried to drive the Uí Ímair <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a> under Sitric Cáech from Ireland. The Vikings won decisively, and Niall and five other Irish kings were killed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niall-glundub">Niall Glúndub</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1115">1115 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">911 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Roger of Salerno routs a Seljuk army at Sarmin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The crusader army of Roger of Salerno, regent of the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a>, surprised and routed the numerically superior Seljuk Turkish army of Bursuq ibn Bursuq of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamadan">Hamadan</a> at Sarmin, also known as Tell Danith.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1141">1141 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">885 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Matilda of Boulogne's army routs Empress Matilda at Winchester</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The army of the imprisoned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephen-king-of-england">King Stephen</a>, led by his queen, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matilda-i-countess-of-boulogne">Matilda of Boulogne</a>, blockaded Empress Matilda's forces at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winchester">Winchester</a> and crushed them as they retreated. Robert of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gloucester">Gloucester</a> was captured and exchanged for Stephen, who regained the throne.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matilda-i-countess-of-boulogne">Matilda of Boulogne</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephen-king-of-england">Stephen</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winchester">Winchester</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1321 CE <span class="tih-ago">705 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Dante Alighieri dies in exile in Ravenna</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dante-alighieri">Dante</a> died in Ravenna, months after finishing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/divine-comedy">Divine Comedy</a>. Written in Tuscan rather than <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a>, his poem helped make that dialect the basis of the Italian language.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1812">1812 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">214 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon's army enters Moscow</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grande-armee">Grande Armée</a> entered a largely deserted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, and fires soon destroyed much of the city. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> waited five weeks for a peace offer that never came before beginning his disastrous retreat.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grande-armee">Grande Armée</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/theodore-roosevelt" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/theodore-roosevelt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1901">1901 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">125 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">McKinley dies and Theodore Roosevelt becomes president</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-mckinley">William McKinley</a> died of gangrene from his gunshot wounds. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodore-roosevelt">Theodore Roosevelt</a>, aged 42, became the youngest president in US history.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1982">1982 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">44 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Princess Grace of Monaco dies after a car crash</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Former film star Grace Kelly died a day after her car left a mountain road above Monaco. She had given up Hollywood to marry Prince Rainier III in 1956.</p></div></li></ol>
